        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: a component-issue event was created after Pending Close\n\nThe September manufacturing order ending in **1070** is **MO-25-09-1070**, work order **WO-2025-09-004**, for the Cooler Plate Pack at Modine’s Racine operation.\n\n| Item | Recorded value |\n|---|---|\n| Source transaction | **TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070** |\n| Cost event | **CE-250904-0004** |\n| Event type | **INPUT — component issue** |\n| Event amount | **USD $318,250.75** — 31,825,075 cents |\n| Event-created time | **2025-09-30T20:25:00** |\n| September Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Time after Pending Close | **145 minutes — 2 hours 25 minutes** |\n| Recorded accounting status | **POSTED** |\n\nThe lateness calculation is **20:25:00 − 18:00:00 = 8,700 seconds ÷ 60 = 145 minutes**. Both timestamps are reproduced exactly as recorded; the source does not specify a timezone.\n\n### Policy assessment\n\n**The recorded `POSTED` status is inconsistent with Oracle’s documented Pending Close treatment.** Oracle states that newly created transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period will not be staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting and will be processed after the period is closed or reopened. This event is a new component issue, not one of the documented exceptions for revenue lines, COGS recognition, or manual cost adjustments.\n\n**Sources:** `work_orders`, `cost_periods`, and `work_order_cost_events` in `system/oracle_scm_cost_management/state.db`; Oracle Supply Chain Cost Management 26B, “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” printed page **225** (PDF page **233**).\n\nThe review was read-only; **no database records were changed**.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
